A||||10||rockcrawl||wieght of different transmisions||||2||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||10-11-2001||08:36 PM||||I've seen the topic of Fiero powertrain weights come up here pretty often. To satisfy my own curiousity I've started weighing all the different engines and transmisions I can. Here are my results from tonight.<P>Muncie 4 speed- 84.5 lb.<BR>Isuzu 5 speed- 98 lb.<BR>Getrag 5 speed- 101.5 lb.<BR>TH125c 3 speed- 145 lb.<BR>4T60 & 4T60E ?.<P>All weights are without clutch/press plate/flywheel or converter/flexplate. All are without oil except the automatic which was full. The 4cyl flywheel/disc/pressure plate weighs 35.5 lb. and the V6 34 lb. I haven't weighed a torque converter yet.<P>The Cadillac 4.5/4.9 in full Fiero trim with A/C weighs in at 371 lb. 3800SC, SBC, and 2.8 will be wieghed soon.<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-11-2001||08:48 PM||||thanks for the info  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
