Z||000003||terryk||10-11-2001||09:37 PM||||4T60EHD is 210 pounds.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||10-11-2001||10:49 PM||||Bob and Terry, thanks for the additions. Are those dry weights? With or without converter? I'll have a chance to weigh a 4T60 and a 4T60E, as well as several different engines. I'm trying to get an 'apples for apples' comparasin of all the different choices. If I weight them here I can use the same scale and make sure they all have the same hardware attached.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gerald||10-12-2001||03:32 PM||||Hey, seeing how your doing this any way how about weighing a 2.0 turbo. Id really like to know the weight savings i could get.<P>Thanx<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||10-12-2001||04:58 PM||||I'm 95% sure that is with the TC. When one got shipped, they removed the TC to get it under 200 lbs for the carrier.<P>Checkout <A HREF="http://www.gmpowertrain.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpowertrain.com</A>....<P>For the 4T65E<P>205 lb (93.6 kg) M15, MD7 <BR>212 lb (96.6 kg) MN3  <BR>214lb (97.2 kg)MN7  <P>4T60E is pretty much the same. <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||1
